.TH LINT 1
.SH NAME
lint \- check the text of source files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lint
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Lint
checks each file against the text rules of PliCad and prints
.IB file : line :
and the fault for each one found.
.PP
Files are ASCII, with no carriage returns, no trailing blanks, and a
final newline.
Files with comments, except the Makefile and dot files, begin with
three comment lines and a blank line
(the SPDX identifier,
.RI \(dq name " -- " description \(dq,
and the copyright; after a #! line, lines 2 to 4).
Markdown and data files
.RB ( .expected ,
.BR .fold ,
.BR .step ,
.BR .json )
have no header.
Lines other than C are at most 80 columns, with tabs to multiples
of 8; Markdown link definitions, table rows and URLs are exempt.
C has no block comments, no typedefs of structs,
and no #if, #ifdef or #ifndef inside a function.
.PP
In comments and Markdown prose, spaced dashes are not allowed
(a -- or a hyphen between words of three letters or more,
except in the header line, in lines that begin with a hyphen,
and in quotes),
and PliCad is spelt in lower case only in paths, file names and
commands.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 1 if a fault is found.
